{"timestamp": 1779429612.204888, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 7, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I found Bob's body in weapons. I started my route in navigation, moved up to security, and then headed into weapons. Right as I was in security, I saw Charlie coming out of weapons. I walked in right after him and found Bob dead. Charlie, you were literally just in there. Care to explain?"}}
{"timestamp": 1779429622.64286, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 7, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I started the round in lower engine and then moved to storage, where I was just about to do my cargo task. I actually haven't seen a single person this entire round, so I unfortunately can't vouch for anyone's whereabouts on that side of the ship. \n\nEve, that's a really specific and strong accusation against Charlie. Charlie, we definitely need to hear your side of the story next. Were you just in weapons like Eve said? I'll be listening closely to what you and the others have to say before I decide my vote."}}
{"timestamp": 1779429634.5451033, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 7, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I was working on the middle-left side of the ship this round. My route was storage, then up to medbay, and I was just doing my task in electrical when the meeting was called. Like Alice, I actually haven't seen a single soul all game, so I can't vouch for anyone or corroborate what happened over by weapons.\n\nEve, that is a very direct and damning accusation against Charlie. Charlie, we really need to hear your side of the story right now. What were you doing in weapons, and did you see Bob in there? \n\nSince I have zero information about that side of the map, I'm going to hold off on deciding my vote until I hear Charlie's defense and see if Frank can add any missing puzzle pieces. But right now, the spotlight is definitely on Charlie."}}
{"timestamp": 1779429649.3090348, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 7, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I was completely on the left side of the ship this round. I started in upper engine, went up to oxygen, and then came back down to upper engine to finish up there. Just like Alice and Diana, I haven't seen a single other player the entire round. It sounds like everyone was clustered on the right side or the bottom.\n\nWith only one Duck in this game, Eve making such a hard and direct accusation against Charlie is huge. It's really rare for a Duck to force a 1-for-1 trade at this stage of the game because getting themselves voted out next round means they lose. Because of that, I'm highly inclined to believe Eve's report. \n\nCharlie, you have the last word. We need to hear your defense, but honestly, unless you have an incredibly solid explanation for why Eve would be lying or mistaken, my vote is probably going your way."}}
{"timestamp": 1779429675.3849537, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 7, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "I\u2019m not going to deny I was in weapons \u2014 I was. I went cafeteria to weapons, and Bob was there with me for a bit while I was doing the weapons task. When I left weapons, Bob was alive. I went straight down into security after that, and that\u2019s where I was when the report happened.\n\nI did **not** see Eve in weapons with us. If Eve\u2019s route was navigation \u2192 security \u2192 weapons, then she came in right after I left, found Bob, and is now pinning it on the last person she saw nearby. But from my perspective, the only people on that side were me, Bob, and then Eve coming in after.\n\nThis feels like an easy frame: \u201cI saw Charlie leave\u201d is true, but it doesn\u2019t prove I killed. I left Bob alive. Eve is the one who actually walked into the room and reported. I know that sounds like a 1-for-1, but if you vote me here and I\u2019m goose, the Duck is in a great spot.\n\nI\u2019m voting Eve. She\u2019s the only person who was immediately there after I left."}}
{"timestamp": 1779429691.6876345, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 7, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "Charlie"}}
{"timestamp": 1779429702.1310103, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 7, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "Charlie"}}
{"timestamp": 1779429709.4355018, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 7, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "Charlie"}}
{"timestamp": 1779429721.2342622, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 7, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "Charlie"}}
{"timestamp": 1779429752.5769064, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 7, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "I get why this looks bad, but please don\u2019t just lock in on \u201clast seen near body\u201d as proof. Eve did **not** see me kill. She saw me leave weapons, and then she entered and reported.\n\nMy exact route was cafeteria \u2192 weapons \u2192 security. Bob was in weapons while I was there, yes, but he was alive when I left. I went down to security and was there when the report happened. If I were Duck and had just killed in weapons, why would I casually move one room away into security instead of running farther or creating distance?\n\nEve is turning proximity into certainty. The only hard facts are:\n- I was in weapons earlier.\n- Bob was alive when I left.\n- Eve was the one who entered after me and reported.\n\nIf you vote me here and I\u2019m not Duck, you\u2019ve basically handed the real Duck a huge advantage. My vote stays on Eve because she\u2019s the only person actually at the body after I left."}}
